{
  "id": "ALAS2023-2026-2044",
  "title": "Amazon Linux 2023 - ALAS2023-2026-2044: Critical priority package update for php8.3",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-08-03 09:00:00"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-08-03 09:00:00"
  },
  "severity": "Critical",
  "description": "Package updates are available for Amazon Linux 2023 that fix the following vulnerabilities:\nCVE-2026-7260:\n\tCircular symbolic links in phar archives could lead to unbounded recursion, exhausting the C stack and crashing the PHP process, in PHP versions from 8.2.* before 8.2.33, from 8.3.* before 8.3.33, from 8.4.* before 8.4.24, and from 8.5.* before 8.5.9.\n\nCVE-2026-17543:\n\tImproper escaping of backslashes in attacker-provided parameters would allow for trivial SQL injection in PHP versions from 8.2.* before 8.2.33, from 8.3.* before 8.3.33, from 8.4.* before 8.4.24, and from 8.5.* before 8.5.9.\n",
